 "caption": "Someone has one question for you. They open your contact form and find eleven boxes: surname, company, postal code, date of birth.\n\nThey fill in one, scroll, and close the tab. Not because they changed their mind about you. Because asking was more work than it was worth.\n\nTo answer a new customer you need three things: a name, a way to reach them, and what they want. Everything else can wait until you're actually talking.\n\nNo website yet? The same rule applies wherever people reach you: keep the first step small.\n\nHow many fields does your contact form have?"
